WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.966
Follow a requirement from intended
function

2
00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:06.534
through a possible failure to the evidence
needed.

3
00:00:06.654 --> 00:00:09.275
For the fictional heating control, ask

4
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:12.429
whether the requirement concerns
indication,

5
00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:16.204
control stability, alarm response or
heater shutdown.

6
00:00:16.324 --> 00:00:19.704
One generic check saying temperature
satisfactory

7
00:00:19.824 --> 00:00:22.444
does not establish all four functions.

8
00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:26.220
Assign distinct observations where the
claims differ.

9
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.012
Write the criterion before collecting
results.

10
00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:32.891
State the challenge, starting condition,

11
00:00:33.011 --> 00:00:36.666
measurement method, time basis and
expected response.

12
00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:39.958
For example, a response-time requirement
needs

13
00:00:40.078 --> 00:00:43.300
an identifiable initiating event and
endpoint.

14
00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:47.006
An observed delay cannot become its own
limit simply

15
00:00:47.126 --> 00:00:50.091
because the first test produced that
value.

16
00:00:50.711 --> 00:00:54.918
In one teaching record, the input event
occurs at ten o clock

17
00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:58.686
and the defined output follows 3.2 seconds
later.

18
00:00:58.806 --> 00:01:01.921
The hypothetical protocol limit is 4
seconds.

19
00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:05.753
The observed 3.2 seconds meets that simple
limit.

20
00:01:05.873 --> 00:01:08.425
Timestamp resolution, clock alignment

21
00:01:08.545 --> 00:01:13.303
and the prescribed decision method must
still support the comparison.

22
00:01:13.923 --> 00:01:18.337
If the result misses the criterion,
preserve it and investigate.

23
00:01:18.457 --> 00:01:22.319
Changing the limit afterwards to make the
result pass is

24
00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:24.439
not a defensible shortcut.

25
00:01:24.559 --> 00:01:29.801
A scientifically justified change requires
the appropriate documented route,

26
00:01:29.921 --> 00:01:31.926
impact assessment and review.

27
00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:34.322
The original criterion and failed

28
00:01:34.442 --> 00:01:37.407
observation remain traceable in the
record.
